# Exact root row payload for orientation 0

Certificate `e7987d7fa66008d497e31c976c68f025d57664a145336d358328375cc5738ca3`.

**Zero entries are dropped.**  `weightedEntropyList` sums its argument and adds one Shannon
summand per entry, and a zero entry contributes neither, so deleting zeros changes no value; the
committed `DyadicEntropyForm.weightedEntropyForm_dropZeros` family is the statement of that.  The
dense rows carry 523,184 integers across all orientations and only 49,854 nonzero ones, so the
sparse serialization is what makes this payload representable at all.

**Semantic-handoff caveat, recorded for the acceptance audit.**  These rows are a *generated
encoding* of the certificate's root law.  Nothing here proves that they are the reconstruction of
that law from the committed `TotalQuotientPrimary*` tables — that identification is a separate,
still-open obligation.  It is open in exactly the same way for the committed level-four analytic
payload, whose `branchRate` likewise reads generated cached tables rather than the primaries (see
the honest note in `TotalWeightEndpointLevelFourSpecialization`); the root side is not stronger,
and must not be read as stronger.
